The sliding window pattern is closely related to two pointers. Instead of moving two pointers independently, you maintain a window (a subarray or substring) and expand or shrink it to satisfy a condition.

1. Maximum Sum Subarray of Size K
Problem

Given an array and a window size k, find the maximum sum of any contiguous subarray of size k.

Time Complexity: O(n)

2. Longest Substring Without Repeating Characters
Problem

Find the length of the longest substring without repeating characters.

Window: always contains unique characters.

3. Minimum Size Subarray Sum
Problem

Find the smallest length of a contiguous subarray whose sum is greater than or equal to target.

Key idea: Expand until valid, then shrink to find the minimum window.

